{% extends "layout/gates.twig" %}

{# ── COLOUR BUDGET: tier 1, and the one event is the honour band ───────────────
   A decided edition is one of exactly two page types allowed to cash their single
   tile in for a full-bleed field — the other is the hall of fame. That is the
   rarest thing on this platform getting the loudest treatment, and it is
   enforceable because it is a list of two.
   Every other status on the page is unpainted: a withheld award is an OUTLINE and
   never a fill, because on a page that is mostly good news the absence of one
   result must not be the loudest thing on it. See ColourBudgetTest. #}
{% set colour_tier = '1' %}
{# The privilege is DECLARED and the declarations are counted, because "only two page
   types may do this" is only safe as a list of two — a band arrives on a third page one
   defensible page at a time. See ColourBudgetTest::test_the_band_privilege_is_still_a_list_of_two. #}
{% set colour_band = true %}

{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ONE EDITION, AS AN ANNOUNCEMENT
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The overall standing leads, because it is the answer to the click. Somebody
  arriving here has asked "who won this year", and a grid of equal-weight cards
  gives the eye nowhere to land and makes them assemble the answer themselves.

  ── WHAT CHANGED, AND THE ONE THING THAT DID NOT ─────────────────────────────

  This used to be a headline card and a wall of portraits, and it could not say
  three things a reader needs: who came second and third in the EDITION (a fact
  that exists nowhere else on the site), which awards in this edition are still
  being checked, and which are still being marked. The category rows carry all
  three, in the same status vocabulary `/results` uses one level up — one
  resolver, never two. See Services\ResultStatus.

  What did not change is the face. `gates_nominees.photo_path` existed for years
  and no result surface ever selected it, so an awards platform for African
  excellence showed its winners as text. A person is the story and the index is
  the evidence for it, so the band keeps a portrait beside the name — a departure
  from the handoff's two-column band, taken deliberately rather than by accident.

  ── THE ARITHMETIC IS NOT HERE ───────────────────────────────────────────────

  Only the split: this much came from people, this much from the panel. That is
  the claim itself rather than a step in a calculation. Everything that produced
  the two figures is on the award's own page, folded away. A reader who wants to
  check a community half can; a family looking for a name should not have to read
  a denominator first.
#}

{% set top = e.top %}

{% block head_styles %}
<style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
  body[data-page="results"]{ background:var(--ag-ground); color:var(--ag-ink); }
  html{ scroll-padding-top:72px; }

  .ed{ max-width:1120px; margin:0 auto;
       padding:clamp(1.5rem,4vw,2.2rem) var(--ag-gutter,32px) clamp(3rem,6vw,4.5rem); }

  .ed-crumb{ margin:0 0 16px; font-size:14px; line-height:1.5; color:var(--ag-ink-soft); }
  .ed-crumb a{ color:var(--ag-ink-2); text-decoration:none; }
  .ed-crumb a:hover{ text-decoration:underline; }
  .ed-crumb b{ color:var(--ag-ink); font-weight:600; }

  .ed-pg{ margin:0 0 10px; display:flex; align-items:center; gap:8px;
          font:600 11px/1.3 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.16em; text-transform:uppercase;
          color:var(--pg-ink,var(--ag-ink-soft)); }
  .ed-pg i{ flex:none; width:9px; height:9px; border-radius:50%; font-style:normal;
            background:var(--pg-fill,currentColor); }
  .ed h1{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700;
          font-size:clamp(2rem,4.8vw,2.9rem); line-height:1.04; letter-spacing:-.03em; }

  .ed-figs{ display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:0 clamp(26px,5vw,50px);
            margin:clamp(1.3rem,3vw,1.9rem) 0 0; padding:0 0 clamp(1.1rem,3vw,1.5rem); }
  .ed-figs dt{ margin:0 0 4px; font:600 11px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.16em;
               text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ag-ink-soft); }
  .ed-figs dd{ margin:0; font:700 clamp(1.35rem,3vw,1.7rem)/1 var(--ag-font-mono);
               letter-spacing:-.02em; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .ed-rule{ height:2px; background:var(--ag-ink); }

  /* ══ THE BAND — the page's one colour event ═══════════════════════════════
     A field, never a line. `honour` is 1.65:1 on paper, which is under the 3:1 a
     border owes and far under the 4.5:1 a word owes, so it is only ever visible
     as a wash with house ink on it — `honour-wash` holds ink above 12:1, which
     SlotFloorTest re-derives rather than trusts. */
  .ed-band{ margin:clamp(1.6rem,4vw,2.2rem) 0 0; padding:clamp(1.5rem,3.4vw,2.1rem) clamp(1.4rem,3vw,2.5rem);
            background:var(--ag-honour-wash); border:1px solid var(--ag-honour-edge);
            border-radius:18px; }
  .ed-band__in{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,1fr) 300px; gap:clamp(18px,3vw,32px);
                align-items:center; }
  .ed-ph{ align-self:stretch; min-height:190px; border-radius:12px; overflow:hidden;
          background:var(--ag-surface-2); display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; }
  .ed-ph img{ width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; display:block; }
  .ed-ph span{ font:700 3.4rem/1 var(--ag-font-display); color:var(--ag-ink-2); }
  .ed-ph--none{ position:relative; }
  .ed-ph--none small{ position:absolute; bottom:10px; left:0; right:0; text-align:center;
                      font:600 10px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.12em;
                      text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ag-ink-soft); }

  .ed-cat{ margin:0 0 6px; font:600 11px/1.3 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.14em;
           text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ag-honour-ink); }
  .ed-name{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700;
            font-size:clamp(1.9rem,4.4vw,2.9rem); line-height:1.02; letter-spacing:-.03em; }
  .ed-name a{ color:inherit; text-decoration:none; }
  .ed-name a:hover{ text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:5px; }
  .ed-name a:focus-visible{ outline:3px solid var(--ag-ink); outline-offset:3px; }
  .ed-gloss{ margin:10px 0 0; font-size:14px; line-height:1.55; color:var(--ag-ink-2);
             max-width:46ch; }

  .ed-idx{ text-align:right; }
  .ed-idx b{ display:block; font:700 clamp(2.4rem,5.6vw,3.6rem)/.92 var(--ag-font-mono);
             letter-spacing:-.045em; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; color:var(--ag-ink); }
  .ed-idx b span{ font-size:.34em; letter-spacing:0; color:var(--ag-honour-ink); }
  .ed-split{ display:flex; justify-content:flex-end; gap:22px; margin:12px 0 0; }
  .ed-split dt{ margin:0 0 3px; font:600 10px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.12em;
                text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ag-honour-ink); }
  .ed-split dd{ margin:0; font:700 1.05rem/1 var(--ag-font-mono);
                font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }

  /* 2nd–4th, inside the band and under its own hairline. The edition's own
     standing exists nowhere else on this site — a category page can only say who
     won that category. */
  .ed-also{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:16px 24px;
            margin:clamp(1.2rem,3vw,1.7rem) 0 0; padding:clamp(1.1rem,2.6vw,1.4rem) 0 0;
            border-top:1px solid var(--ag-honour-edge); }
  .ed-also__r{ margin:0 0 4px; font:700 10px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.14em;
               text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ag-honour-ink); }
  .ed-also__n{ margin:0; font-size:16px; font-weight:600; line-height:1.25; }
  .ed-also__c{ margin:3px 0 0; font-size:14px; line-height:1.4; color:var(--ag-ink-2); }
  .ed-also__i{ margin:5px 0 0; font:700 1.25rem/1 var(--ag-font-mono);
               font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }

  /* OUTLINED, never filled — see the budget note at the top of this file. */
  .ed-caveat{ margin:clamp(1.1rem,3vw,1.5rem) 0 0; padding:14px 18px; border-radius:12px;
              border:1px solid var(--ag-caution-edge); font-size:14px; line-height:1.6;
              color:var(--ag-ink-2); max-width:74ch; }
  .ed-caveat b{ color:var(--ag-caution-ink); }

  /* ══ the awards ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .ed-h2{ margin:clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.6rem) 0 2px; font-family:var(--ag-font-display);
          font-weight:700; font-size:1.35rem; letter-spacing:-.02em; }
  .ed-h2 + p{ margin:0 0 12px; font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; color:var(--ag-ink-soft);
              max-width:62ch; }

  .ed-list{ list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; }
  .ed-row{ border-top:1px solid var(--ag-line); }
  .ed-a{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 250px 220px 110px 40px;
         gap:8px 22px; align-items:center; padding:18px 4px; color:inherit; text-decoration:none; }
  .ed-a:hover{ background:var(--ag-surface-2); }
  .ed-a:focus-visible{ outline:3px solid var(--ag-action-edge); outline-offset:-3px; }
  .ed-row h3{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700;
              font-size:1.1rem; line-height:1.25; letter-spacing:-.01em; }
  .ed-a:hover h3{ text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:4px; }

  .ed-st{ display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; min-height:26px; padding:0 10px;
          border-radius:999px; border:1px solid var(--ag-line); background:var(--ag-card);
          font:700 10px/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase;
          color:var(--ag-ink); }
  .ed-st--counting{ background:var(--ag-live-wash); border-color:var(--ag-live-edge); }
  .ed-st--counting i{ flex:none; width:9px; height:9px; border-radius:50%; font-style:normal;
                      background:var(--ag-live-fill); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference){
    .ed-st--counting i{ animation:ed-pulse 2s ease-in-out infinite; }
  }
  @keyframes ed-pulse{ 0%,100%{ opacity:1 } 50%{ opacity:.45 } }
  .ed-st--withheld{ border-color:var(--ag-caution-edge); color:var(--ag-caution-ink); }
  .ed-st--decided{ border:0; padding:0; background:none; color:var(--ag-ink-soft); }

  .ed-bar{ height:6px; border-radius:999px; background:var(--ag-line); overflow:hidden;
           max-width:170px; margin:8px 0 0; }
  .ed-bar span{ display:block; height:100%; background:var(--ag-ink-2); }
  .ed-sub{ margin:6px 0 0; font:600 10px/1.3 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.08em;
           text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ag-ink-soft);
           font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }

  .ed-won{ min-width:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700; font-size:1.02rem;
           line-height:1.25; margin:0; }
  .ed-quiet{ margin:0; font-size:14px; line-height:1.5; color:var(--ag-ink-soft); max-width:26ch; }
  .ed-n{ text-align:right; font:700 1.35rem/1 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:-.02em;
         font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .ed-n small{ display:block; margin:4px 0 0; font:600 10px/1 var(--ag-font-mono);
               letter-spacing:.1em; color:var(--ag-ink-soft); }
  .ed-go{ text-align:right; color:var(--ag-mute); font-size:18px; }

  .ed-note{ margin:clamp(2rem,4vw,2.6rem) 0 0; padding:18px 20px; border:1px dashed var(--ag-line);
            border-radius:14px; font-size:14px; line-height:1.65; color:var(--ag-ink-2);
            max-width:72ch; }
  .ed-note a{ color:var(--ag-ink); }

  @media (max-width:900px){
    .ed-band__in{ grid-template-columns:120px minmax(0,1fr); }
    .ed-idx{ grid-column:1 / -1; text-align:left; }
    .ed-split{ justify-content:flex-start; }
    .ed-also{ grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr); }
    .ed-a{ grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 200px 40px; }
    .ed-won, .ed-quiet, .ed-n{ grid-column:1 / -1; text-align:left; }
  }
  @media (max-width:560px){
    .ed-band__in{ grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr); }
    .ed-ph{ min-height:220px; }
    .ed-a{ grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 34px; padding:15px 4px; }
    .ed-a > *{ grid-column:1; }
    .ed-go{ grid-column:2; grid-row:1; }
  }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block structured_data %}
{# An award result is the most linkable thing this platform produces and the most
   searched — "who won the 2026 principal awards" is a real query with a real answer.
   Every value goes through `|json_encode`, which escapes `</script>`: a winner's name is
   operator-entered text and `layout/gates.twig` renders this block with
   JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES, which is precisely how a campaign title once closed a script
   element on this site. #}
<script nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}" type="application/ld+json">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"ItemList",
 "name":{{ (e.programme ~ ' ' ~ (e.edition ?: e.year) ~ ' winners')|json_encode|raw }},
 "numberOfItems":{{ e.awards|length }},
 "itemListElement":[{% for a in e.awards %}{"@type":"ListItem","position":{{ loop.index }},
   "item":{"@type":"Person","name":{{ a.winner.name|json_encode|raw }},
     "url":{{ (_site_url ~ a.url)|json_encode|raw }},
     "award":{{ (a.category.title ~ ' — ' ~ e.programme ~ ' ' ~ (e.edition ?: e.year))|json_encode|raw }}}}{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}{% endfor %}]}
</script>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="ed">
  <p class="ed-crumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/results">Results</a> /
     <b>{{ e.programme }} {{ e.edition ?: e.year }}</b></p>

  <div style="{{ e.programme_style }}">
    {# The dot is decoration; the programme's name is the fact, printed beside it always. #}
    <p class="ed-pg"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ e.programme }}</p>
  </div>
  <h1>{{ e.edition ?: e.year }}</h1>

  {# Counted from the drawn edition, never typed: a headline figure written into a
     template is a figure that is wrong the first week an award is added. #}
  <dl class="ed-figs">
    <div><dt>Awards</dt><dd>{{ e.categories|length }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Decided</dt><dd>{{ e.awards|length }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Votes counted</dt><dd>{{ e.votes|default(0)|number_format }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Nominees</dt><dd>{{ e.nominees|default(0)|number_format }}</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <div class="ed-rule"></div>

  {% if top %}
    <div class="ed-band" data-celebrate="edition-{{ e.slug }}">
      <div class="ed-band__in">
        <span class="ed-ph{{ top.winner.photo ? '' : ' ed-ph--none' }}">
          {% if top.winner.photo %}
            <img src="{{ top.winner.photo|media_url('portrait') }}" alt="{{ top.winner.name }}"
                 width="420" height="525" loading="eager" decoding="async">
          {% else %}
            {# No photograph is common and is not an error, so it is never a broken-image
               frame. `aria-hidden` on the initial: announcing "O" before the person's own
               name reads as a stammer. #}
            <span aria-hidden="true">{{ top.winner.name|slice(0,1)|upper }}</span>
            <small>No photograph</small>
          {% endif %}
        </span>

        <div>
          {# The tile: a bounded field with a saturated mark and a WORD inside it. The word
             is what carries the meaning — cover the gold and this still reads. #}
          <span data-celebrate-anchor>
            {% include 'partials/tile.twig' with {
                 meaning: 'overall-winner', size: 'lg',
                 label: 'Highest index this edition'
               } only %}
          </span>
          <p class="ed-cat" style="margin-top:12px">{{ top.category.title }}</p>
          <h2 class="ed-name"><a href="{{ top.url }}">{{ top.winner.name }}</a></h2>
          {% if e.overall and e.overall.margin is not null and e.overall.margin > 0 %}
            <p class="ed-gloss">Clear of second in the edition by {{ e.overall.margin }}{% if e.awards|length > 1 %},
              across {{ e.awards|length }} awards{% endif %}.</p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>

        <div class="ed-idx">
          <b>{{ top.winner.cpi }}<span> / 1000</span></b>
          {# THE SPLIT, AND NOTHING ELSE. Not a step in a calculation — it is the claim
             itself: this much came from people, this much from the panel. #}
          <dl class="ed-split">
            <div><dt>Community</dt><dd>{{ top.winner.community_points }}</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Panel</dt><dd>{{ top.winner.judge_points }}</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>

      {% set also = e.overall.top4|default([])|slice(1, 3) %}
      {% if also|length %}
        <div class="ed-also">
          {% for c in also %}
            <div>
              <p class="ed-also__r">{{ loop.index + 1 }}{{ loop.index + 1 == 2 ? 'nd' : (loop.index + 1 == 3 ? 'rd' : 'th') }} in the edition</p>
              <p class="ed-also__n">{{ c.name }}</p>
              <p class="ed-also__c">{{ c.category }}</p>
              <p class="ed-also__i">{{ c.cpi }}</p>
            </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {% if e.overall and e.overall.provisional %}
      {#
        Naming somebody "highest in the edition" and then quietly replacing them when a
        withheld award lands is worse than saying it is not settled. The caveat is about
        OUR process and says so — it is never a mark on the person it sits under.
      #}
      <p class="ed-caveat"><b>Provisional.</b>
        {{ e.overall.held }} award{{ e.overall.held == 1 ? '' : 's' }} in this edition
        {{ e.overall.held == 1 ? 'is' : 'are' }} still being checked, and the top of the
        edition can change when {{ e.overall.held == 1 ? 'it lands' : 'they land' }}. Every
        award already decided is final. The caveat is about our process, not about the
        people named here.</p>
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}

  <h2 class="ed-h2">The awards in this edition</h2>
  <p>Every award, decided or not. Open a decided one for the full standing — every nominee
     who scored, in the order the award was decided — and the working behind it.</p>

  <ul class="ed-list">
    {% for c in e.categories %}
      <li class="ed-row">
        {# The whole row is the link where there is one; the chevron is an affordance
           marker, never the target. An undecided award has nowhere to go yet, and a link
           to nothing is worse than no link. #}
        {% set tag = c.url ? 'a' : 'div' %}
        <{{ tag }} class="ed-a"{% if c.url %} href="{{ c.url }}"{% endif %}>
          <h3>{{ c.title }}</h3>

          <div>
            <span class="ed-st ed-st--{{ c.status.key }}">
              {% if c.status.key == 'counting' %}<i aria-hidden="true"></i>{% endif %}
              {{ c.status.label }}
            </span>
            {% if c.progress %}
              {# A count against its own denominator — the one honest ramp here, because it
                 is a statement about OUR work rather than about a person. The figure is
                 written out as well as drawn: a bar with no number is a picture of
                 progress rather than a statement of it. #}
              <div class="ed-bar" role="progressbar" aria-valuemin="0"
                   aria-valuemax="{{ c.progress.needed }}" aria-valuenow="{{ c.progress.done }}"
                   aria-label="Scorecards in for {{ c.title }}">
                <span style="width:{{ c.progress.pct }}%"></span>
              </div>
              <p class="ed-sub">{{ c.progress.done }} of {{ c.progress.needed }} scorecards in</p>
            {% endif %}
          </div>

          {#
            `publishes_standing`, not the status name: adding a fifth status must not be
            able to open this column by accident. No leader is published for an award while
            its voting is open, at any level.
          #}
          {% if c.status.publishes_standing and c.award %}
            <p class="ed-won">{{ c.award.winner.name }}</p>
            <p class="ed-n">{{ c.award.winner.cpi }}<small>/ 1000</small></p>
          {% elseif c.status.key == 'withheld' %}
            <p class="ed-quiet">Decided, and being checked before it is published.</p>
            <p class="ed-n" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</p>
          {% else %}
            <p class="ed-quiet">No standing while this award is open.</p>
            <p class="ed-n" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</p>
          {% endif %}

          <div class="ed-go" aria-hidden="true">{{ c.url ? '→' : '' }}</div>
        </{{ tag }}>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <p class="ed-note">
    Nothing is announced until the whole index can be shown: the community half, the
    judges' half, and the working behind both. How an index is built, and what money can
    and cannot move, is set out in full on <a href="/integrity">integrity</a>.
  </p>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block foot_scripts %}
{% if top %}{% include 'partials/celebrate.twig' only %}{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
